{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Levodopa\", \"id\": \"D007980\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ocular dyskinesias\", \"id\": \"D015835\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"Parkinson's disease\", \"id\": \"D010300\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"Levodopa\", \"id\": \"D007980\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ocular dyskinesias\", \"id\": \"D015835\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"choreatic dyskinesias\", \"id\": \"D002819\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"levodopa\", \"id\": \"D007980\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"levodopa\", \"id\": \"D007980\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ocular dyskinesias\", \"id\": \"D015835\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Levodopa","id":"D007980","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"ocular dyskinesias","id":"D015835","label":"Disease"},{"text":"Parkinson's disease","id":"D010300","label":"Disease"},{"text":"choreatic dyskinesias","id":"D002819","label":"Disease"}],"head":"Levodopa","head_id":"D007980","pairs":[{"head":"Levodopa","tail":"ocular dyskinesias","head_id":"D007980","tail_id":"D015835"},{"head":"Levodopa","tail":"Parkinson's disease","head_id":"D007980","tail_id":"D010300"},{"head":"Levodopa","tail":"choreatic dyskinesias","head_id":"D007980","tail_id":"D002819"}],"relations":["D007980 | D015835","D007980 | D002819"],"result":"$","tail":"choreatic dyskinesias","tail_id":"D002819","text":"Levodopa-induced ocular dyskinesias in Parkinson's disease. Levodopa-induced ocular dyskinesias are very uncommon. Usually they occur simultaneously with limb peak-dose choreatic dyskinesias. We report on a patient with leftward and upward deviations of gaze during the peak effect of levodopa, and hypothesize that a severe dopaminergic denervation in the caudate nucleus is needed for the appearance of these levodopa-induce ocular dyskinesias.","metrics":{"precision":0.5,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.6666666666666666,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":0}}